        "chapterId": 422,
        "headingId": 469,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T11:52:50"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 707,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 470,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107525,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 422,
        "headingId": 470,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T11:52:50"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 708,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 471,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107526,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 422,
        "headingId": 471,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Sclerosing stromal tumour occurs in the ovary; rarely, it is paraovarian {26327562}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T11:52:50"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 709,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 472,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107527,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 422,
        "headingId": 472,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Patients present with menstrual abnormalities, abnormal uterine bleeding, or abdominal pain. Precocious puberty {9522851; 19604650; 24686794; 30577720}, virilization {21829415; 30577720}, and an association with ascites (Meigs syndrome) {15285324; 20925634} have occasionally been reported. Most tumours are unilateral, but bilateral cases have been described {16403568; 26064755}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T11:52:50"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 710,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 473,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107528,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 422,
        "headingId": 473,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Sclerosing stromal tumours account for 7&ndash;28% of all sex cord stromal tumours in childhood and adolescence {12910419; 24606464}. They typically occur in adolescents and young women (median age: 29&nbsp;years) {19071970; 31896750} but can also arise in premenarchal girls as well as in infants as young as 7&nbsp;months {17990931; 18358265; 24656709}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T11:52:50"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 711,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 474,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107529,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 422,
        "headingId": 474,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T11:52:50"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 712,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 475,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107530,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 422,
        "headingId": 475,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>GLI2</em> rearrangements have been detected in &gt;&nbsp;80% of sclerosing stromal tumours, with the <em>FHL2</em>::<em>GLI2</em> fusion being present in &gt;&nbsp;60% of cases {31896750}. No recurrent mutations have been identified.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T11:52:50"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 719,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 482,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107531,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 422,
        "headingId": 482,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Tumours range in size from 15&nbsp;to 190&nbsp;mm (mean: 110&nbsp;mm) {4348335; 20135135; 27149006; 28982854}. They are well circumscribed, often with a yellow to white cut surface that may show central oedema and cyst formation.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T11:52:50"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 713,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 476,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107532,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 422,
        "headingId": 476,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Sclerosing stromal tumour has a pseudolobular appearance and a prominent vasculature, typically composed of thin-walled dilated vessels with a haemangiopericytoma-like appearance. Pseudolobules are separated by a hypocellular oedematous, collagenous, or (occasionally) myxoid stroma. Cellular nodules are composed of an admixture of bland epithelioid and spindled cells. The former have clear to eosinophilic vacuolated cytoplasm, sometimes resulting in a signet ring&ndash;like appearance {4348335}, and may show prominent luteinization, especially during pregnancy {25851706}. Mitotic activity is often low, but large numbers of mitoses are seen in a small subset of cases {27149006}. Tumours are usually positive for sex cord markers, such as inhibin, calretinin, and FOXL2, but are negative for cytokeratins and EMA.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T11:52:50"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 714,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 477,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 107533,
        "bookId": 44,
        "chapterId": 422,
        "headingId": 477,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-03-09T11:52:50"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 715,
    "bookid": 44,
    "headingType": 2,
